    {
        "k":  "h2",
        "runs":  [
                     {
                         "t":  "9. FAQs",
                         "b":  false
                     }
                 ]
    },
    {
        "k":  "p",
        "runs":  [
                     {
                         "t":  "Q: Is a photofacial painful?\n",
                         "b":  true
                     },
                     {
                         "t":  "Ans. Most people describe a warm snapping feeling with each pulse. It\u0027s usually well tolerated, and numbing cream generally isn\u0027t needed.",
                         "b":  false
                     }
                 ]
    },
    {
        "k":  "p",
        "runs":  [
                     {
                         "t":  "Q: Is there any downtime?",
                         "b":  true
                     },
                     {
                         "t":  " \nAns. Not really. You may look slightly pink for a few hours, and spots can darken briefly before flaking off.",
                         "b":  false
                     }
                 ]
    },
    {
        "k":  "p",
        "runs":  [
                     {
                         "t":  "Q: How many sessions will I need?",
                         "b":  true
                     },
                     {
                         "t":  " \nAns. Usually around five, spaced 3 to 4 weeks apart. Many people see improvement by the second or third session.",
                         "b":  false
                     }
                 ]
    },
    {
        "k":  "p",
        "runs":  [
                     {
                         "t":  "Q: Is it safe for Indian skin?",
                         "b":  true
                     },
                     {
                         "t":  " \nAns. Yes, as long as the settings are adjusted for darker skin tones. That\u0027s an important part of the assessment.",
                         "b":  false
                     }
                 ]
    },
    {
        "k":  "p",
        "runs":  [
                     {
                         "t":  "Q: Can a photofacial treat rosacea?",
                         "b":  true
                     },
                     {
                         "t":  " \nAns. Yes. It targets the small blood vessels behind persistent redness, and improvement builds over a course of sessions.",
                         "b":  false
                     }
                 ]
    },
    {
        "k":  "p",
        "runs":  [
                     {
                         "t":  "Q: Will my brown spots go away completely?",
                         "b":  true
                     },
                     {
                         "t":  " \nAns. Many people see them fade a lot. Complete clearance depends on the type and depth of pigment and on sun protection.",
                         "b":  false
                     }
                 ]
    },
    {
        "k":  "p",
        "runs":  [
                     {
                         "t":  "Q: How long do the results last?",
                         "b":  true
                     },
                     {
                         "t":  " \nAns. A year or more with good sun protection and a suitable skincare routine. An annual maintenance session helps.",
                         "b":  false
                     }
                 ]
    },
    {
        "k":  "p",
        "runs":  [
                     {
                         "t":  "Q: What does a photofacial cost in Delhi?",
                         "b":  true
                     },
                     {
                         "t":  " \nAns. A single full-face session is around ₹4,000 to ₹8,000, and a course of five is about ₹18,000 to ₹35,000. The final price is confirmed at your consultation.",
                         "b":  false
                     }
                 ]
    },
    {
